    },
    "Use selection for find" : {

    },
    "Use Selection for Find" : {

    },
    "View ▸ Enter Focus Mode (⌥⌘F) hides the sidebar and inspector and empties the toolbar, narrows the cards to a reading width and dims every block but the one you're in. Typewriter Scrolling (⌥⌘T) keeps the line you're typing at the centre of the window. View ▸ Editor Theme sets all of Kisho — editor, sidebar and inspector — to light, dark or sepia independently of the system; the Format menu has Bold, Italic, Underline and Document Font presets." : {

    },
    "View ▸ Show Inspector (⌥⌘I) opens a panel for the selected block: a status (Draft, Revised, Final, Done), one of eight colours, a synopsis and private notes. The sidebar shows the colour as a dot and the status as a small symbol, and View ▸ Show Synopses puts each synopsis under its title — so the sidebar doubles as an outline you can plan in. Notes are never exported." : {

    },
